{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-q554-3cjc-rx7p","cve_id":null,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/security-advisories/GHSA-q554-3cjc-rx7p","html_url":"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/security/advisories/GHSA-q554-3cjc-rx7p","summary":"Component-model handle tables are capped only per instance and charged to no limit","description":"### Summary\r\n\r\nA malicious guest can drive unbounded host memory growth using only component-model resource handles, with no linear memory, no core tables, no host imports, and default configuration.\r\n\r\n### Impact\r\n\r\nEach guest `resource.new` allocates a slot in the owning component instance's host-side handle table. Allocation is bounded only by a per-table cap and is charged to no `ResourceLimiter` or `StoreLimits`, so `-W max-memory-size` and the embedder's configured memory and table limits do not bound it. Because the cap is per component instance, a single component can exceed it many times over by instantiating a sub-component repeatedly.\r\n\r\n## Patches\r\n\r\nWasmtime 49.0.3, 48.0.6, and 36.0.18 have been fixed by introducing a store-wide limit on the number of simultaneously-live component-model handles.\r\n\r\n- Default limit: **100,000 live handles per store** (~2.4 MB of handle-table memory).\r\n- New embedder knob: `Store::set_max_component_handles(n)` to raise or lower it.\r\n- New CLI flag: `-S max-component-handles=N` for `wasmtime run` / `wasmtime serve`.","severity":"medium","author":null,"publisher":{"login":"alexcrichton","id":64996,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0OTk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64996?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton","html_url":"https://github.com/alexcrichton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-q554-3cjc-rx7p","type":"GHSA"}],"state":"published","created_at":null,"updated_at":"2026-10-14T17:25:27Z","published_at":"2026-10-14T17:25:27Z","closed_at":null,"withdrawn_at":null,"submission":null,"vulnerabilities":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"rust","name":"wasmtime"},"vulnerable_version_range":"<36.0.18, >= 37.0.0, <48.0.6, >=49.0.0, <49.0.3","patched_versions":"49.0.3, 48.0.6, 36.0.18","vulnerable_functions":[]}],"cvss_severities":{"cvss_v3":{"vector_string":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","score":6.2},"cvss_v4":{"vector_string":null,"score":null}},"cwes":[{"cwe_id":"CWE-400","name":"Uncontrolled Resource Consumption"},{"cwe_id":"CWE-770","name":"Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling"}],"cwe_ids":["CWE-400","CWE-770"],"credits":[{"login":"tschneidereit","type":"reporter"},{"login":"fitzgen","type":"remediation_developer"}],"credits_detailed":[{"user":{"login":"tschneidereit","id":56359,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MzU5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56359?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tschneidereit","html_url":"https://github.com/tschneidereit","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tschneidereit/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tschneidereit/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tschneidereit/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tschneidereit/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.c